Text: (2019) as a single language model pre-trained on the concatenation of mono- lingual Wikipedia corpora from 104 languages.1 M-BERT is particularly well suited to this probing study because it enables a very straightforward ap- proach to zero-shot cross-lingual model transfer: we ﬁne-tune the model using task-speciﬁc super- vised training data from one language, and evalu- ate that task in a different language, thus allowing us to observe the ways in which the model gener- alizes information across languages.

